vents":[],"summary":{"sentences":["Revolve Group, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Retail-Catalog & Mail-Order Houses\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 6 years.","It reported $1.2bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 15.6% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 52.7%.","Listed on NYSE, it funds itself from operations ($181.8m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 15.6% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $342.9m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Gross margin of 52.7% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $181.8m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Net cash of $335.8m against total assets of $821.4m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.1% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526206542/0001193125-26-206542-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-206542"}],"bear":[{"text":"Insiders disposed of 83.2% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (440,825 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526263764/0001193125-26-263764-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.1% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1746618/000119312526263764/0001193125-26-263764-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 45.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.45,"consecutive":2,"current":0.527,"current_display":"52.7%","threshold_display":"45.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 1.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.01,"consecutive":2,"current":0.156,"current_display":"15.6%","threshold_display":"1.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label"